.el .ds Aq '
.TH temporal-tui-auth 1  "auth "
.SH NAME
temporal\-tui\-auth \- Sign in to a protected self\-hosted Temporal deployment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtemporal\-tui auth\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign in to a protected self\-hosted Temporal deployment
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Alternate config file. Defaults to the platform user config directory
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Named connection profile
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
temporal\-tui\-auth\-login(1)
Sign in with a local username and a password read without echo
.TP
temporal\-tui\-auth\-whoami(1)
Show the current signed\-in identity and session status
.TP
temporal\-tui\-auth\-logout(1)
Revoke the refresh grant and remove its local credential
